{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "איש על דגלו באתת", :translit "ish al diglo be'otot", :gloss "each man by his banner, by signs"} {:he "שיעקב רמז להם", :translit "sheya'akov remaz lahem", :gloss "that Jacob hinted to them"} {:he "מי יהיה ראש דגל", :translit "mi yihyeh rosh degel", :gloss "who would be head of a banner"} {:he "כל מי שדבר עמו לנוכח", :translit "kol mi she-diber imo le-nokhach", :gloss "whoever he spoke with face-to-face"} {:he "היה ראש דגל", :translit "hayah rosh degel", :gloss "would be head of a banner"} {:he "ראובן בכורי אתה", :translit "re'uven bekhori atah", :gloss "Reuben, you are my firstborn"} {:he "יהודה אתה יודוך", :translit "yehudah atah yodukha", :gloss "Judah, you—your brothers shall praise you"} {:he "יוסף מאל אביך ויעזרך", :translit "yosef me-el avikha veyiazrekha", :gloss "Joseph—may El your father help you"} {:he "דן לישועתך קויתי ה'", :translit "dan li-yshu'atekha kiviti Hashem", :gloss "Dan—I wait for Your salvation, YHWH"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Direct address in Jacob's blessings identifies each tribal banner leader"}], :frame {:text "Jacob's blessings to his sons in Genesis 49 contain direct address to Reuben (Genesis 49:3), Judah (Genesis 49:8), Joseph (Genesis 49:25), and Dan (Genesis 49:18). Each of these four tribes headed one of the four encampment banners described in Numbers 2.", :sources ["Genesis 49:3" "Genesis 49:8" "Genesis 49:25" "Genesis 49:18" "Numbers 2:3" "Numbers 2:9" "Numbers 2:18" "Numbers 2:25"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מנגד סביב לאהל", :translit "minneged saviv la-ohel", :gloss "opposite, surrounding the Tent"} {:he "לאלפים אמה", :translit "le-alafim amah", :gloss "to thousands of amah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מנגד סביב לאהל", :b "לאלפים אמה"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "סביב לאהל מועד יחנו והחנים", :translit "saviv le-ohel mo'ed yakhenu veha-khanim", :gloss "Surrounding the Tent of Meeting they shall encamp, and those encamping"} {:he "כשם שחנייתן למעלה ד' דגלים סביב לכסא הכבוד", :translit "k'shem she-khanyatan le-ma'lah dalet degalim saviv la-kisse ha-kavod", :gloss "just as their encampment above is four banners surrounding the Throne of Glory"} {:he "כך היה למטה ד' דגלים סביב למשכן", :translit "kakh hayah le-matah dalet degalim saviv la-mishkan", :gloss "so below it was four banners surrounding the Tabernacle"} {:he "איומה כנדגלות", :translit "ayumah ke-nidgalot", :gloss "awesome as bannered companies"} {:he "ודגלו עלי אהבה", :translit "ve-diglo alai ahavah", :gloss "His banner over me is love"} {:he "שישראל ראו בשעת מתן תורה הדגלים של מעלה", :translit "she-yisra'el ra'u be-sha'at matan Torah ha-degalim shel ma'lah", :gloss "for Israel saw at the time of the giving of the Torah the banners above"} {:he "ונתאוו לאותן הדגלים", :translit "ve-nit'avu la-otan ha-degalim", :gloss "and yearned for those banners"} {:he "ובשם אלהינו נדגול", :translit "u-ve-shem Eloheinu nadgol", :gloss "and in the name of our God we will set up banners"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Correspondence: four earthly camps around the Tabernacle mirror four heavenly banners around the Throne of Glory"}], :frame {:text "The verse Songs 6:4 'awesome as bannered companies' (איומה כנדגלות) is read as a description of the four camps surrounding the divine Throne. Songs 2:4 'His banner over me is love' (ודגלו עלי אהבה) is connected to Israel's vision at Sinai. Psalms 20:8 'and in the name of our God we will set up banners' (ובשם אלהינו נדגול) is applied to Israel's earthly encampment. Midrash Tanchuma states that four camps of ministering angels corresponding to the four tribal standards descended at Sinai, and Israel desired banners like them (Numbers Rabbah 2:3).", :sources ["Songs 6:4" "Songs 2:4" "Psalms 20:8" "Numbers Rabbah 2:3" "Tanchuma Bamidbar 12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Direct address in Jacob's blessings identifies each tribal banner leader", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "מנגד סביב לאהל", :a-value 237, :b "לאלפים אמה", :b-value 237, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Correspondence: four earthly camps around the Tabernacle mirror four heavenly banners around the Throne of Glory", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:53.924491567Z", :model "glm-5.2"}